# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTO-GENERATED by Claude Code
# Purpose: Everything about showing a Python value (DataFrame, pydantic model, match videos, ...)
#          in the app, for agent tool results, cell outputs and tabs alike. Two matches:
#            to_view(value)          Python `match` on the value's type -> View (runs when a cell
#                                    or tool returns; View.data() is what the browser gets)
#            render_component(view)  rx.match on ViewData.kind -> the component (compiled into
#                                    the page; the browser never sees the Python object, hence
#                                    the two steps)
# Usage: view = to_view(value)   -> None when the value has no view (shown as its repr)
#        render_component(State.view, State.view_event)
#        Add a type: a `case` in to_view; a new kind of view also needs a `case` in
#        render_component. No State import here (state.py imports this file).
# Rule:  a value renders as ONE contained component, the same wherever it is placed (a tab, a
#        cell output, a popup, ...). Everything that belongs to it (a table's filter and sort,
#        a video list's player and paging) is inside what render_component returns, and its
#        state travels in its ViewData. A host only says where the view lives (its slot, eg
#        "tab:r1", "cell:c3") and gives one event handler; it adds nothing of the view's own.
#        compact only changes sizing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
